        "text": "Answers\n1.I White-box testing\n2.I Mock objects help simulate the behavior of external or internal dependencies. By\nusing mock objects, we can focus on writing tests for validating functional behavior.\n3. setUp , tearDown , setUpClass , tearDownClass\n4.I TDD is an approach to developing software by writing the test cases first. CI is a\nprocess in which all the tests are executed every time we build a new release. There\nis no direct relationship between TDD and CI.\n5.I DDT is used when we have to do functional testing with several permutations of\ninput parameters. For example, if we are required to test an API endpoint with a\ndifferent combination of arguments, we can leverage DDT.",
